#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""static-npc STEP ID [options]: the green path for a static NPC - a figure that stands in one place and never walks - as
bound Gaussian splats (Patch 2026-11-22; the route is docs/splat-scaffold.md "Static NPCs", first run on 021).

ID is the CMS id, npc-NNN (Patch 2026-11-22: clearer; 017 and 021 came before it with bare numbers). The bake's run inside
work/ keeps the bare number (work/NNN/A, bake id NNN-A), as the batch scripts read run ids as NNN-X; publications are named
npc-NNN-bound-....

Walkers too (npc.json "walker": true; init --walker; npc-468, 2026-11-23, Patch: the animated NPC process in the same
manner): Meshy's API rig with donor hands in place of the short chain, the stick guide from that rig, and after bound a walk
step (skirt bones for a robe or long skirt, the Mixamo clips on the bench, tidy) in place of the static idle. The steps that
differ say so below.

Every file lives in the character's folder, local/art/generated/people/dagger-characters/ID/:
  00-brief/      npc.json (settings) and the prompts, edited by hand for each character: clay-front.txt, clay-back.txt,
                 orbit.txt (the orbit clip), rings.json (the three repaint rings and their negatives). init copies 021's as a start.
  01-concept/    approved/{front,back}.png from the rusty-dagger CMS (back optional: with none, front_only in npc.json, every
                 step takes the front alone and the orbit's back is H3's own; Patch 2026-11-22, 023); wip/cut, wip/keys-1920
  02-guide/      wip/clay, wip/mesh-clay, wip/orbit-guide (stick joints, guide videos); scaffold/scaffold.glb (the short rig)
  work/          the bake's run folder: work/NNN/A/{guided,bake,bound}
  08-final, 09-game   the bound bake and its runtime sizes, filed by dagger-char bound (publish)

Steps, in order (each checks that the one before it has run):
  init      dagger-char init, the approved front (and back, if approved) from the CMS (--cms, default ID), npc.json, prompt templates
            Experiment (npc-471, 2026-11-25): init --from DIR with a side.png too (a three-view sheet split in three; --side right|left),
            or right.png and/or left.png (a four-view sheet: npc.json "sides"; they follow the back as <Picture 3>, <Picture 4>; the clip
            scales the references to 1280 px, npc.json "ref_size", so four fit the GPU lab at 1920)
            sets npc.json "side": keys, clay (00-brief/clay-side.txt), Meshy and the orbit take it as a third view (<Picture 3>), and
            "side_guide": true also pins it at its frame of the orbit
  keys      cut both paintings from their background (flood_cut, --tolerance) and make the 1920 px keyframes
  clay      Qwen edits both keyframes to plain grey clay on the GPU lab (00-brief/clay-*.txt)
  mesh      Meshy multi-view mesh of the clay pair, untextured (20 credits); on a content block, local Hunyuan3D-2mv instead
            (Patch 2026-11-22), or --mesher hy2mv from the start
  rig       walker: meshy_rig.py (Meshy's remesh and API rig of the mesh's task, 10 credits; when Meshy can't estimate the pose, or
            with npc.json "rigger": "fit", asset-pipeline's fit_rig.py fits the target rest pose's skeleton to the mesh and weights it
            by bone heat on a watertight proxy - npc-468's pose-locked painting, 2026-11-24) and transplant_hands.py (rigged donor
            hands at the cuffs, DONOR_HANDS) -> scaffold.glb with 36 joints, and scaffold_views.py's check renders.
            static: static_rig.py: the short chain (Hips..Head, still hands) and the stick-figure joints for the guide, turned to the
            paintings' view when they are drawn at an angle (measured from the outlines; npc.json "view_yaw" overrides; 017).
            npc.json "hands": front (held before the body, the default), sides (hanging at the thighs: 023) or 'X,Y,Z;X,Y,Z'.
            Look at the guide's first frames before the clip: the stick's arms are what H3 poses the arms by
  guide     the lit stick-figure and depth orbit guide (Blender on den-m5); a walker's stick comes from its rig (stick_fit.py)
  clip      H3 REF2VA orbit clip on the GPU lab (00-brief/orbit.txt), --size 1920 by default
  bake      cut-outs, cameras, first fit, the repaint rings (00-brief/rings.json) and round-1 data; stops before the free
            round-1 fit (npc.json bake_to "r1data"; batch 2 showed the bound bake does not need it). About 50 min.
  bound     the bound bake (400k) and each runtime size in npc.json "sizes" (default 32k: one figure, never a crowd), cleaned
  preview   static, optional: the procedural idle and look clips rendered from six views (bound_run.sh idle)
  r1        optional, for a graft: the free round-1 fit of a bake that stopped at r1data (bake --to r1 does it in one go)
  graft     optional: the free r1 fit grafted on the face and hands of each runtime size (graft_free.py, CPU) -> size NNk-graft,
            which publish then shows beside the plain size (npc.json "graft": regions, default "face,hands"; "graft_face_cone", 45).
            Patch shipped npc-023 so (2026-11-23): the bound bake blurs where Meshy's clay is a poor stand-in (mitten hands)
  hands     walker, optional, after graft: turn_hands.py re-rests open, palm-forward painted hands (along the forearm, thumb forward)
            so the clips start from a natural hand (npc-468)
  walk      walker: for each runtime size (and its graft): skirt (npc.json "skirt": skirt bones, two-tier XPBD, for a robe or long
            skirt), the Mixamo Walking and Around clips on the GPU lab, tidy (drop_loose.py: Gaussians that come loose in the clips),
            and the clips again on the tidied body for the review stills. Sizes NNk-face-share-cleaned[-skirt]-tidy, NNk-graft[-skirt]-tidy
  publish   dagger-char bound ID: adopt, playable (idle and look clips from static_idle.py), publish to the Workbench
  ship      after Patch's look: --size NAME --said "his words". The chosen size becomes 09-game/bound/final (dagger-char bound
            choose: ID.glb with the eye mask, ID-idle.glb, ID-look.glb, ready.json), the matte inset core beside it (core_extract.py:
            ID.core.glb with the core as a second primitive, rusty-engine #10990's contract; ID-core.glb for the Workbench;
            npc.json "core_tris", default 2400 as on npc-023, 0 for none), the overview page, and the CMS link to the character
  status    which steps have their outputs
  sync      write the CMS stage states (#pipelines) from what is on disk; every other step keeps them current as it runs

Hosts: npc.json "gpu_host" (or --gpu) puts every GPU step - clay, clip, bake's lab stages and VACE rings, r1, bound, walk - on a
Strix Halo (den-m5 or den-nimo) instead of the GPU lab (Patch 2026-11-24: lengthy work on a Halo when he needs the 5090). The CPU
stages run on npc.json "cpu_host" (default den-m5) either way.

Gate for Patch: the bake in the Workbench after publish (no clip gate since 2026-11-22: clips haven't been rejected in a long time). Long steps
(clip, bake, bound) run in the foreground for tens of minutes: run them under authoring/tools/people/splat/bake/watchdog.sh.
"""
